Z||000000||Homicidal||05-05-2000||01:19 AM||||I can't understand it.......I just can't get it.<P>The car has such a hard start now, it barely makes it, sputtering and dying.  And after it's started, it drives great, but I feel a slight bucking when hitting the HI rpm's of a gear (3 1/2-4000).<P>I drive the car for a bit, and then when I try to start it again, it starts d@mn near perfect.<P>Occasionally when I start the car the lights flicker on and off, which would point to a battery.  But it just doesn't feel electrical.<P>But I also get a lot of exhaust and some water spitting out my exhaust pipe.  Could that be water in the engine which would mean a cracked engine block/head?  Would a car even start and run with a cracked block??<P>I am just so lost.  I don't know WHERE to start to fix this friggin problem.||||reg||5
Z||000001||batboy||05-05-2000||01:51 AM||||More likely a cracked head, if something is really cracked (or blown head gasket). The key here: are you losing coolant? Radiator level lower than last time you checked? Is the exhaust smoke white or does it have a blue tint or is it dark and sooty?||||reg||1
