Z||000006||theogre||05-05-2000||09:39 AM||||This is a 4 isn't it? Check the head bolts on the front side. They have a habit of breaking or stretching bad. GM wanted them replaced durring recall work, especially on the 84's, but few dealers likely did it.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Luperman||05-05-2000||10:58 PM||||Have you done a compression check yet on the cylinders thats a good way to tell if you have a cracked head or block..||||reg||5
Z||000008||zeusrekning||05-05-2000||11:07 PM||||Homicidal, do we own the same car? I'm not having the same problem as you but i am was having problems. We have spent $350 on my clutch problem this month. clutch, master cylinder, slave cylinder(not added b/c i returned it),starter,oil,timing gears,air filter, oil filter,plugs.<BR>just recently put on new tires and alternator/battery.<BR>Still think the clutch was not installed properly.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Racer 1||05-06-2000||12:23 AM||||<B>99.98</B> its a blown head gasket or leaky head gasket. Go down to a auto store and get some radiator leak stopper comes in a tube and looks like quick silver. I had the same problem when I put my new head gasket on and got everything back together I had the infamous <B>"WHITE CLOUD"</B> I put the stop leak in and the white smoke went away 4 good.||||reg||9
Z||000010||Phaeton||05-06-2000||05:46 AM||||Oh yeah, smokin' loosens me right up, not tense at all I'm not,<BR>Forget that water burning crap, water don't burn, its those alternator bearings being too tense, not wanting the engine to turn over, but why isn't your belt squealing?<P>You really getting white smoke all the time without losing water?  Has it been especially humid in the area lately? <P>Does the oil look like dirty whipped cream has been added? Rainbows in the water?<P>Hmmm, what is the tach doing while the lights are flickering?<P>Tripped codes weren't mentioned so I ass u me there aren't any.  Ditto for less than shiny connections on any electric cable terminals.<P>Is the hard start related to how warm the starter assembly is? Is the starter solenoid making good contact only when hot?<P>Questions.  More questions.  Getting too untense, glad I don't have to drive anywhere tonight.||||reg||12
